  "rationale": "A wins (97, ahead of C at 92 and B at 84) because it is the most complete. It handles velocity with explicit units, a projected endpoint and a separate velocity handoff. It interrupts from the sampled presentation position and velocity, and it rejects conflicting transform ownership outright. Its evidence labels are also the most careful. C is close but leaves out velocity units and comes closer to predicting how the sheet will feel at runtime. B labels some runtime consequences as observed and treats velocity projection only briefly.",
