        "motion_necessity": 8,
        "performance": 10,
        "velocity_projection": 15
      },
      "score": 97,
      "summary": "Labels static evidence, risks and proposed moves strictly, and makes no runtime claims. It covers lockout, pointer capture, grab offset, 1:1 tracking and a jump-free threshold. On interruption, it samples presentation position and velocity and guards against stale callbacks. It gives velocity in CSS px/s with unit conversion, separates projection from the velocity handoff, and states snap-selection policy. It explicitly separates transform ownership. Reduced Motion and the runtime plan come with acceptance gates. The case for removing motion as unnecessary is a little less explicit than in C."
    },
